x86_64-linux  The C1 and D1 forms, and nothing else: `_ZN1BC1Ev`, `_ZN1BD1Ev`, `_ZN1DC1Ev`, `_ZN1DD1Ev`, `_ZN1TC1EPFidE`, `_ZN6HolderC1EPFiiE`. clang emits only the base-object C2 and D2 forms where no base is virtual and calls C2 at the complete-object site; cxx1 emits both, as cleanup.nonames records. Every function the argument picks - `_Z1hi`, `_Z1hd`, `_Z1hii`, `_ZN1n1qEi` and the member functions behind `&S::g` and `&B::g` - agrees with clang letter for letter. x86_64-windows agrees on all 45 names.
arm64-darwin  the same C1 and D1 forms, the two Itanium targets emitting these the same way as each other.
